# Review: MapPlugin

The plugin is largely built: the `Map` type, the create-object entry that builds a `ViewModel` with a
pivot field, the built-in view `MarkerProvider`, the `map` companion gated on a matching provider, the
MapTiler/OSM tile switch from the `apiKeys` setting, and marker selection dispatching
`LayoutOperation.Select` all exist. Almost nothing is tested beyond activation (`plugin.test.ts`,
`MapPlugin.workerd.test.ts`) and one storybook smoke story, so most verdicts are `untested`.

The divergences: `createMap` is not an operation (creation is a `CreateObjectEntry`), `toggleMapView`
takes a required `{ type }` instead of flipping, `Map.coordinates` is used only as the globe's tour
route rather than as static markers, and `MapViewEditor` neither persists a changed typename nor
writes a field id into `pivotFieldId` (it writes the property name, which the marker provider then
fails to match). The skill has no tools and a one-line instruction.

## Extensions

| Term      | URI                        |
| --------- | -------------------------- |
| `verdict` | `org.dxos.mdl.verdict@1.0` |

## Verdicts

```mdl
verdict GeoPoint: The plugin uses echo's `Format.GeoPoint`, a [lng, lat] tuple.
  status: untested
  evidence: [github:dxos/dxos/packages/plugins/plugin-map/src/types/Map.ts#Map]
  note: There is no plugin-local GeoPoint; `Map` fields use `Format.GeoPoint` from `@dxos/echo`, stored as [lng, lat] and read that way in `useViewMarkers`.
```

